```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Starting : user runs fx ask
    Starting --> ErrorResultWritten : fails before first model step (bad flags, missing auth)
    Starting --> Running : run_started written to event sink

    Running --> ModelStreaming : model request starts (step_start emitted)
    ModelStreaming --> RecoveryWait : transient failure (recovery emitted, ticker armed)
    RecoveryWait --> ModelStreaming : wait expires (resend)
    ModelStreaming --> ParallelTools : model calls tools (step_end emitted)
    ParallelTools --> ParallelTools : tool finishes out of order (tool_start/tool_end emitted)
    ParallelTools --> Running : all tools in batch finish

    ModelStreaming --> Finalizing : model finishes final answer (step_end emitted)
    Finalizing --> Done : run_finished to sink + exact --json result on stdout

    Running --> Cancelling : SIGTERM arrives
    ModelStreaming --> Cancelling : SIGTERM arrives
    RecoveryWait --> Cancelling : SIGTERM arrives
    ParallelTools --> Cancelling : SIGTERM arrives
    Finalizing --> Cancelling : SIGTERM arrives

    Cancelling --> CancelledBroken : [current / mutant-buffered / mutant-skip-cancel] events buffered or cancel dropped (violates NoEventLostOnSigterm)
    Cancelling --> DoneCancelled : [design-a / design-b] cancel event flushed, prior events kept

    Running --> Killed : SIGKILL arrives (all prior flushed event lines remain valid JSONL)
    ModelStreaming --> Killed : SIGKILL arrives
    ParallelTools --> Killed : SIGKILL arrives

    note right of CancelledBroken
        Shortest path to broken NoEventLostOnSigterm (current-sigterm):
        Starting -> Running -> Cancelling -> CancelledBroken (exit 143, empty stdout).
        Other broken mutants:
        - mutant-unlocked: parallel tool B races tool A -> ValidJsonPerLine
        - mutant-no-final: Finalizing omits final JSON -> FinalResultMatchesJson
        - mutant-file-abort: Design B event file ENOSPC aborts turn -> FileFullDoesNotAbortTurn
        - mutant-stdout-clobber: Design B writes events to stdout -> IgnoreEventsGetsResult
    end note
```

Events omitted from chart to keep <= 20 arrows:
- `SinkFails` (stdout closed/full in Design A stops emitting; event file full in Design B latches and continues stdout)
- `TickerEmit` (concurrent recovery/notice refresh serialized under mutex)
- `SIGKILL` from `RecoveryWait`, `Cancelling`, and `Finalizing`
